    "definitions": {
      "short": "a community",
      "usage": "nation, people.",
      "full": "H3816. leom לְאוֺם לְאֹם, noun masculine Gen 25:23 people , in poetry and chiefly late; — ׳ל absolute 25:23 (twice in verse); Prov 14:28 , לְאוֺם 11:26 ; suffix לְאוּמִּי Isa 51:4 ; plural לְאֻמִּים Gen 25:23 28 t.; לְאוּמִים Isa 55:4 ; &#8212; people , both of Israel and of Edom, Gen 25:23 (3 t. in verse) (J; Jacob and Esau; || גּוֺי ); elsewhere of Israel only Isa 51:4 (singular || עַם ); usually plural of other peoples: — ל ׳שְׁאוֺן 17:12 (|| עמים הֲמוֺן , compare 17:13 ; || גּוֺיִם 34:1 ; 43:9 ; Psa 2:1 ; 44:3 ; 44:15 ; 105:44 ; 149:7 , compare Isa 55:4 (twice in verse) ( גּוֺי in 55:5 ); || עַמִּים Gen 27:29 (J), Hab 2:13 ; Jer 51:58 ; Psa 47:4 ; 57:10 ; 67:5 (twice in verse); 108:4 ; Prov 24:24 ; further Isa 41:1 ; 49:1 (both || אִיִּים ), 43:4 (|| אָ֯דָם 60:2 (|| אֶרֶץ ), Psa 9:9 (|| תֵּבֵל ), 148:11 (|| אֶרֶץ מַלְכֵי , etc.); לְאֻמִּים עֲדַת 7:8 , ל ׳הֲמוֺן 65:8 ; of any and all peoples Prov 14:34 ; singular indefinite = people in General, as making public opinion, 11:26 (collective, with plural verb); = population , as subjects of prince 14:28 (|| עַם ).",
      "rootNote": "or לְאוֹם ; from an unused root meaning to gather ;",
